# L §7.3: "Where the exact value is a rational on a cell edge, the engine detects it exactly: perfect powers,
# exp(0), ln(1)"; such a value isn't widened, so it prints plain (The error bound).  exp(0) = 1, ln(1) = 0,
# sqrt(4) = 2, pow(4, 0.5) = 2, each on its step's grid.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input four: num
input half: num
def ex: num = exp(0) to 0.1 at reader
def lx: num = ln(1) to 1e-9 at reader
def sq: num = sqrt(four) to 1 at reader
def pw: num = pow(four, half) to 1e-3 at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  four = 4
  half = 0.5

ask a: ex, lx, sq, pw law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: (1, 0, 2, 2)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
